In article <21973@rnd.GBA.NYU.EDU> kichin@rnd.GBA.NYU.EDU (Kirby Chin) writes:
>
>
>I was playing nethack 3.0j on a IBM 286AT and my game crashed.  I was a 12th
>level Valkyrie on level 25.  My character was wandering around and the keyboard
>just froze and my key buffer jammed up.
>
>Has anyone ever experienced the same problem?

Yes.  I have experienced this many times.
>
>If so, is it possible to revive the game and how?

There is no way to revive the game.  To avoid having further problems, go
to your bones directory and delete all the level.* files, so that future games
won't think that you are cheating.
>
>... and since we're on the topic of crashes...
>I've also had a game crash when I prayed once (ctrl-p) and the game kicked me
>to a DOS print prompt.  I said somelike like...
>
>Writing Device Error:
>Abort, retry, fail?
>
>and I lost my entire game.  Is this an old bug or what?

This is not really a bug.  It's that the PC thinks that you want to start
printing.  Keep pressing ^P and r, and eventually you will get out of it.

